course: dictionary
lesson: 6823
title: Other: one small word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word other is small, but it does a lot of jobs. It can mean a different one, as in «the other side of the road». It can mean the rest of a group, as in «the other children». Read the words next to it to see which job it is doing.
explain: Look for clues around other. In «each other», the two words go together to mean one another. In «the other day», other means a few days ago. The words that come next often tell you the meaning.
explain: Try swapping in a different word. In «The other children went home early», you can ask: would «the rest of the children» fit? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Other means a different one, not this one.
fact: «The other» or «the others» means the rest of a group.
fact: «Each other» means one another: «They help each other.»
fact: «The other day» means a few days ago, and «other than» means except.
fact: The formal words «remaining» and «remainder» mean the same as the others when you talk about what is left.
exercise: «The other children went home early.» What does other mean here? | Children with coats | A group of children who were loud | Children who were ill | *The rest of the children
exercise: «They always help each other.» What does each other mean? | *One another | Against each other, as in a fight | Far away from each other | Only two people
exercise: «I saw him the other day.» When did you see him? | On the other side of town | *A few days ago | Every single day | Tomorrow
test: «Other than the dog, nobody came to the party.» What does other than mean? | *Except | Beside | Before | Also
test: Which is a stiff, formal word for the others? | Wobbly | *Remaining | Happy | Nearby
exam: «Each bottlenose dolphin has its own signature whistle, which others copy to call it.» What does others mean here? | Its own calf | Old friends only | Silent fish | *Other dolphins
